# Do Not Commit Without Explicit Request

Do **not** run `git commit`, `git commit --amend`, or create commits in any other way unless the user **explicitly** asks you to commit.

If it is unclear whether the user wants a commit, **ask first** rather than committing proactively.

## Allowed without explicit request

- Read-only git inspection (`git status`, `git diff`, `git log`).

Staging rules are defined in `no-stage-without-explicit-ask.mdc`. An explicit commit request still permits staging as part of that commit workflow.

## Requires explicit user request

- Any command that creates or rewrites commits (`git commit`, `git commit --amend`, empty commits).

Do **not** amend unless the user explicitly requests it and other safety conditions from existing git rules are met (e.g. commit not pushed).
